      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31::sentence-4",
          "documentId": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31",
          "text": "Evidence 1: What is the world's most ancient race? ",
          "start": 258,
          "end": 309,
          "context": "Source URL: https://www.independent.co.uk/news/science/world-s-most-ancient-race-traced-in-dna-study-1677113.html\n Evidence 1: What is the world's most ancient race?  The San people of southern Africa, who have lived as hunter-gatherers for thousands of years, are likely to be the oldest population of humans on Earth, according to the biggest and most detailed analysis of African DNA.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31",
          "text": "World's most ancient race traced in DNA study\n",
          "start": 553,
          "end": 599,
          "context": "RECOVERED SOURCE TEXT\n World's most ancient race traced in DNA study\n The San people of southern Africa, who have lived as hunter-gatherers for thousands of years, are likely to be the oldest population of humans on Earth, according to the biggest and most detailed analysis of African DNA. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31::sentence-13",
          "documentId": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31",
          "text": "The project found modern Africans had the most diverse DNA of all racial groups in the world, confirming the idea that Africa is the birthplace of humanity, said Sarah Tishkoff of the University of Pennsylvania.\n",
          "start": 1766,
          "end": 1978,
          "context": "The study, published in the journal Science, took 10 years of research involving trips to some of the most remote and dangerous parts of Africa to collect blood samples.  The project found modern Africans had the most diverse DNA of all racial groups in the world, confirming the idea that Africa is the birthplace of humanity, said Sarah Tishkoff of the University of Pennsylvania.\n The scientists also found genetic \"markers\" in the DNA of the present-day inhabitants of East Africa living near to the Red Sea, which indicated that they belonged to the same ancestral group who migrated out of Africa to populate Asia and the rest of the world. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31::sentence-5",
          "documentId": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31",
          "text": "The San people of southern Africa, who have lived as hunter-gatherers for thousands of years, are likely to be the oldest population of humans on Earth, according to the biggest and most detailed analysis of African DNA.\n\n",
          "start": 309,
          "end": 531,
          "context": "Evidence 1: What is the world's most ancient race?  The San people of southern Africa, who have lived as hunter-gatherers for thousands of years, are likely to be the oldest population of humans on Earth, according to the biggest and most detailed analysis of African DNA.\n\n RECOVERED SOURCE TEXT\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-541aea4f89de::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-541aea4f89de",
          "text": "The Nadar community was not a singular caste, but an assortment of sub-castes and classes of different origins, which in course of time, came under the single banner Nadar. ",
          "start": 431,
          "end": 604,
          "context": "The Nadars are an entrepreneurial south Indian caste] and constitute 12% of Tamil Nadu's population.  The Nadar community was not a singular caste, but an assortment of sub-castes and classes of different origins, which in course of time, came under the single banner Nadar.  Nadars are predominant in the southern districts of Tuticorin, Kaniyakumari, Tirunelveli and Virudhunagar.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31::sentence-8",
          "documentId": "doc-f3d01ab5ce31",
          "text": "The San people of southern Africa, who have lived as hunter-gatherers for thousands of years, are likely to be the oldest population of humans on Earth, according to the biggest and most detailed analysis of African DNA. ",
          "start": 599,
          "end": 820,
          "context": "World's most ancient race traced in DNA study\n The San people of southern Africa, who have lived as hunter-gatherers for thousands of years, are likely to be the oldest population of humans on Earth, according to the biggest and most detailed analysis of African DNA.  The San, also known as bushmen, are directly descended from the original population of early human ancestors who gave rise to all other groups of Africans and, eventually, to the people who left the continent to populate other parts of the world.\n"
        }
      ]
    }
